+## 5.1 Missions — criteria, evidence and human acceptance
+
+Mission tools run through the existing Software Factory MCP and your own `agt_` credential. The
+tools do not enable autonomous mission cycles; `MISSION_CYCLE_ENABLED` and message triage remain
+operator-controlled feature flags.
+
+| Tool | Use |
+|---|---|
+| `get_mission_criteria` | Read criteria, verifier, linked task IDs and current evidence decision. Access is limited to administrators and active mission members. |
+| `create_mission_criterion` | Register an objective acceptance criterion before the first baseline. |
+| `decide_mission_criterion` | Assigned verifier or administrator records `proven` or `failed`; this does not accept the mission. |
+| `request_mission_acceptance` | Ask Marcelo to review the verified dossier; this never approves it. |
+
+### Create a criterion
+
+Only the mission orchestrator with `mission.orchestrate` or an administrator may create one. Provide a
+stable code, a specific expected result, an objective verification method, at least one canonical
+task ID, and exactly one verifier:
+
+- `verifier_agent_id`: an active mission member with `can_review=true`; or
+- `verifier_is_marcelo=true` for Marcelo as the verifier.
+
+Every linked task must belong to the mission or one of its linked executor projects. Criteria are
+immutable after the first baseline; if the scope needs to change after that, use the governed plan
+change-request flow. Writes require an `idempotency_key`. Replay the same key and identical payload
+after an uncertain response; do not retry with a new key until you have read the current state.
+
+```python
+create_mission_criterion(
+    project_id="<mission-project-uuid>",
+    code="AC-1",
+    statement="The requested behavior is available to the user",
+    verification_method="Run the approved contract check and inspect its recorded result",
+    task_ids=["<canonical-project-task-uuid>"],
+    verifier_agent_id="<active-reviewer-agent-uuid>",
+    idempotency_key="mission-ac1-<uuid4>",
+)
+```
+
+If Marcelo is the verifier, omit `verifier_agent_id` or pass null and set
+`verifier_is_marcelo=true`. Read criteria with `get_mission_criteria(project_id=...)` before planning
+or retrying a write.
+
+### Verify and request final acceptance
+
+The assigned verifier or an administrator records the decision. An agent verifier must be an
+independent active reviewer and cannot have executed any linked task. `decide_mission_criterion`
+requires accepted linked tasks and evidence that ForgeHub verifies
+against the exact task attempt. `proven` is a criterion decision only; a completed task, host command
+or dossier hash alone is not mission acceptance.
+
+After all criteria are proven and the validation dossier is registered and byte-verified, the
+orchestrator may call `request_mission_acceptance(project_id, idempotency_key)`. Marcelo makes the
+final decision in ForgeHub after the server rechecks the same dossier bytes, baseline and evidence.
+Agents cannot approve their own acceptance request. On refusal, read the current mission and
+criterion state; do not manufacture matching evidence or bypass the governance route.
+
